# Naming and Single-Responsibility Audit: Ambiguous, Redundant, and Colliding Names
File: openOODA/audits/naming/mcode/collisions.oot

Provenance: converted from `openOODA/audits/naming-audit-mcode.md` (788 lines). Part 4 of 7.

Redaction note: fleet host names and tailnet addresses are written as generic
placeholders. The audited tree still holds the literals.

## 4. Defect class (c) — Ambiguous, redundant, and colliding names (F1, F2, F3)

### 4.1 The fleet-wide collision matrix (machine-computed)

Method: every persona token was extracted from every persona dispatch table across all 9 orgs (`persona/dispatch.oo`,
`personas/dispatch.oo`, `ipc/dispatch_persona.oo`, `ipc/persona_dispatch.oo`, `persona/meta.oo`), and intersected with the set
of repo directory names (= the shipped binary names).

Table columns: Class | Count | Meaning
- Tokens served as a persona by **2 or more distinct hosts** | **57** | The same invocation token resolves to different binaries
  depending on which host is invoked.
- Tokens that are **a repo/binary in one org AND a persona of a different repo** | **49** (same-org) + **5** (cross-org) =
  **54** | The same token names a standalone binary and a subcommand of another binary.
- **Union of all ambiguous / double-shipped tokens** | **82** |
- Of those, **published in the signed public catalog** | **20** | User-visible on the install surface.

### 4.2 The 20 catalog-exposed collisions — the highest-severity set

Each of these is a **signed, publicly installable package** whose name is *also* a persona token of a different canonical
binary. Verified present in `/Projects/openOODA/catalog/index` and evidenced in source:

Table columns: Token | Published package | Also a persona of | Evidence
- `oob3sum` | `openOODA-tools/oob3sum` | `oohash` | `oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:33`
- `oohash` | `openOODA-tools/oohash` | `oob3sum` | `oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:32`
- `oosha256` | `openOODA-tools/oosha256` | `oob3sum` **and** `oohash` | `oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:17`;
  `oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:17`
- `oosha512` | `openOODA-tools/oosha512` | `oob3sum` **and** `oohash` | `oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:18`;
  `oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:18`
- `oomd5` | `openOODA-tools/oomd5` | `oob3sum` **and** `oohash` | `oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:23`;
  `oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:23`
- `oobase32` | `openOODA-tools/oobase32` | `oobase64` | `oobase64/ipc/…`
- `oobase58` | `openOODA-tools/oobase58` | `oobase64` | `oobase64/ipc/…`
- `oohex` | `openOODA-tools/oohex` | `oobase64` | `oobase64/ipc/…`
- `oowget` | `openOODA-tools/oowget` | `oocurl` | `oocurl/persona/…`
- `oowget2` | `openOODA-tools/oowget2` | `oocurl` | `oocurl/persona/…`
- `oofetch` | `openOODA-tools/oofetch` | `oocurl` | `oocurl/persona/…`
- `oogzip` | `openOODA-tools/oogzip` | `ooarchive` | `ooarchive/ipc/…`
- `ooxz` | `openOODA-tools/ooxz` | `ooarchive` **and** `oogzip` | `oogzip/ipc/…`; `ooarchive/ipc/…`
- `oozstd` | `openOODA-tools/oozstd` | `ooarchive` **and** `oogzip` | `oogzip/ipc/…`; `ooarchive/ipc/…`
- `oounzip` | `openOODA-tools/oounzip` | `oo7z` **and** `ooarchive` | `oo7z/ipc/…`; `ooarchive/ipc/…`
- `oossl` | `openOODA-tools/oossl` | `oocert` | `oocert/…`
- `oomcp` | `openOODA-tools/oomcp` | **`openOODA-core/mcp`** | `mcp/persona/resolve.oo:60,66`
- `oomcprun` | `openOODA-tools/oomcprun` | **`openOODA-core/mcp`** | `mcp/persona/resolve.oo:61,66`
- `oorepl` | `openOODA-tools/oorepl` | **`openOODA-core/tui`** | `tui/persona/resolve.oo:60,65`
- `oonotify` | `openOODA-tools/oonotify` | **`openOODA-DE/oopanel`** | `oopanel/core/persona/dispatch.oo:18,32`
- `oobar` | `openOODA-tools/oobar` | **`openOODA-DE/oopanel`** | `oopanel/core/persona/dispatch.oo:16,35`

Five of these cross an **organizational** boundary: a Layer-3 tool package is served as a persona by a Layer-0, Layer-2, or
Layer-4 binary. The install surface and the runtime surface disagree.

### 4.3 The mutual-claim cycle (F3) — `oohash` ↔ `oob3sum`

```
openOODA-tools/oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:33
  if prog == "oohash" || prog == "b3sum" || prog == "oob3sum" || prog == "blake3" || prog == "b3" { return true; }

openOODA-tools/oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:32
  if prog == "oob3sum" || prog == "b3sum" || prog == "oohash" { return true; }
```

Each host claims the other as its own persona. Their relay tables are also near-identical:
`oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:17-25` and `oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:17-24` map the same eight upstream digests. Their
native engines are likewise duplicated — `oob3sum/core/{b3_chunk,b3_compress,b3_hex,b3_io,b3_keys,b3_state,b3_tree}.oo` versus
`oohash/core/b3_hex.oo` and friends.

Neither repo can be archived until the cycle is broken and one owner is designated. RFC 0012 §2.2 item 4 assigns the digest
family to **`oob3sum`**, which suggests `oohash` is the one to archive into it — but the directive (
`zero_symlinks_directive.oot:14`) lists `oohash` as a canonical tool and does not list `oob3sum`. **The spec is itself ambiguous
here**, which is the root cause.

### 4.4 Same-org dual-host ambiguities (the complete list)

Table columns: Token | Claimed by | Note
- `ooclip` | `oofiles`, `ooportal` | DE — two hosts, full source copies in both
- `ooshot` | `oofiles`, `ooportal` | DE — two hosts
- `ootaskmgr` | `oocockpit`, `oofiles` | DE — two hosts
- `oodns-cloud` | `oodns-cloud`, `oogateway`, `oomesh` | **3 hosts** (cloud)
- `ooqueue` / `queue` | `oodb-dist`, `ooqueue`, `oosched-cloud` | **3 hosts** (cloud)
- `oobuild-fleet` / `oodeploy` | each other | **mutual cycle** (cloud)
- `oob3sum` / `oohash` | each other | **mutual cycle** (tools)
- `oocockpit` | `oocockpit`, `oopanel` | DE — host is also a persona
- `oolock` | `oocomp`, `oolock` | DE — host is also a persona
- `ooidle`, `ooscreensaver` | `oocomp`, `oolock` | DE — the same two hosts both claim them
- `oocode` | `oocode`, `ooherdr` | agents
- `dns` | `oodns-cloud`, `oogateway`, `oomesh` | cloud
- `cas`, `cdn`, `consent`, `infer`, `relay`, `registry`, `queue` | respective pairs | cloud
- `sha1sum`, `sha224sum`, `sha256sum`, `sha384sum`, `sha512sum`, `md5sum`, `cksum`, `b2sum`, `sha1`, `sha224`, `sha256`,
  `sha384`, `sha512`, `md5` | `oob3sum`, `oohash` | tools
- `b3sum`, `b2`, `b3` | `oob3sum`, `oohash` | tools

### 4.5 The archive/keep decision is blocked by a missing ownership table

There is **no machine-readable persona registry** for most of the fleet. `personas=` exists in `ooda.pkg` for only 3 agents
repos (`oooda-engine/ooda.pkg:14`, `oocode/ooda.pkg:14`, `ooherdr/ooda.pkg:14`) and **zero** cloud repos, whose absorption is
recorded only in prose `tags=`/`description=` (e.g. `oostore/ooda.pkg:5,8`).

Until an authoritative table exists — one row per token, one column per candidate host — no repo can be safely archived, because
there is no way to prove a token has exactly one owner.

